 @Tomatobird8  Well, for 2 years now the only source that keeps calling Arc dead is MLID. He really can't stand how glaringly wrong he was on that and keeps moving the goal posts desperately hoping for the day he can pat himself on the back and say "I told you so." 

A reasonable person would have just admitted they were wrong long ago and move on, but he's got such a massive ego he makes Linus look modestly humble.

I want Arc to continue even if it's just to knock that ego down a peg or twelve and stop being so obviously biased against anyone that's not AMD.

 @Phoenixlul  You can basically forget whatever they say, they have to keep shareholders and employees happy. Those Nvidia GPU tiles are still years away, so they can't just come out now and announce that it's all over. When a product line ends, they just let it fizzle out and die slowly.
Another thing to consider about this partnership, it's super unlikely that Nvidia would hand over any GPU and driver know-how without a non-compete agreement.
I'm afraid it's time to tone down any expectations regarding Arc after Celestial.
